WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Spain occupies the majority of the Iberian Peninsula, blessed with rich Mediterranean coastlines.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Mount Teide on Tenerife rises to 3,715 meters as Spain's highest volcanic peak and UNESCO site.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
In Granada, the Alhambra palace fortress stands as a masterpiece of Moorish Islamic architecture.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Andalusian Flamenco music and dance combine passionate acoustic guitar, cante singing, and castanets.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Traditional culinary heritage features saffron Paella cooked in wide shallow pans in Valencia.

